	"title"		"More Vehicles Renew 2 by NgocDuy"
	"description"		"[h1]🚗 MORE VEHICLES RENEW 2 🚗[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 65K/131K Vehicle Limit Breaker & Simulation Turbo Engine for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Completely modernized, independent, and packed with 4 breakthrough technologies by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🌟 OVERVIEW: MASSIVE CAPACITY EXPANSION[/h1]
Have you noticed that as your metropolis reaches 300,000 - 500,000+ citizens, garbage trucks stop dispatching, cargo delivery vans vanish, and public transit lines run out of available vehicles?
That happens because vanilla [b]Cities: Skylines caps moving vehicles at only 16,384[/b]!

[b]More Vehicles Renew 2[/b] safely pushes the game engine to its absolute mathematical limits:
[list]
[*] [b]Active Moving Vehicles:[/b] [b]65,536[/b] (Vanilla: 16,384) — [b]400% Capacity![/b]
[*] [b]Parked Vehicles:[/b] [b]65,536[/b] (Vanilla: 32,768) — [b]200% Capacity![/b]
[*] [b]Total Vehicles Tracked:[/b] [b]131,072[/b]
[*] [b]Real-World Logistics Throughput:[/b] [b]Equivalent to over 260,000 vehicles![/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]⚡ THE 4 CORE BREAKTHROUGH TECHNOLOGIES[/h1]

[h2]1. 👻 Ghost & Stuck Vehicle Annihilator[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]The Problem:[/b] When you bulldoze or reconfigure congested roads, vanilla and modded games frequently leave 'ghost vehicles' floating in mid-air along the destroyed segments. These orphaned vehicles never reach their destinations and permanently hog thousands of vehicle slots.
[*] [b]The Breakthrough:[/b] Directly hooks [b]NetManager.ReleaseSegmentImplementation[/b] to instantly dissolve any vehicles stranded on demolished segments in real time. In addition, an inline frame-slice watchdog automatically reclaims permanent deadlocks and vehicles with destroyed target destinations.
[/list]

[h2]2. 🚀 Turbo Spawn Dispatcher[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]The Problem:[/b] In vanilla, TransferManager only matches 1 material per frame, meaning after clearing traffic or loading a massive city, it takes 15–20 minutes to respawn vehicles. During this time, commercial stores starve and trigger city-wide economic collapse.
[*] [b]The Breakthrough:[/b] Automatically quadruples (4x) transfer matching when active vehicle demand is high. It cycles through multiple complementary frame phases in a single tick, fully repopulating your city's 60,000 logistics vehicles in just [b]30–60 seconds[/b]!
[/list]

[h2]3. 🛡️ Emergency Slot Reclaimer[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]The Problem:[/b] When vehicle count approaches the 65,535 limit, vanilla CreateVehicle returns false. Factories and shops fail to spawn delivery trucks and abandon with 'Not enough buyers/goods'.
[*] [b]The Breakthrough:[/b] If all 65,535 slots are completely exhausted, the mod automatically reclaims 1 stagnant ghost vehicle in real time, guaranteeing that essential freight, garbage, police, and emergency vehicles [b]always spawn without dropping deliveries[/b].
[/list]

[h2]4. 📦 Smart Logistics Multiplier[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]The Problem:[/b] Metropolises with 500k+ population require 30,000–40,000 delivery trucks just for baseline commercial goods.
[*] [b]The Breakthrough:[/b] Safely doubles the payload capacity of CargoTrucks and GarbageTrucks. Halves the number of freight trucks needed on city streets, effectively giving a 65k vehicle city the logistical throughput of [b]over 260,000 vehicles[/b]!
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]⚠️ COMPATIBILITY & ECOSYSTEM[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Requires CitiesHarmony:[/b] Standard Harmony 2 dependency.
[*] [b]Do NOT Run Concurrently:[/b] Please disable or unsubscribe from original More Vehicles (1764208250) or More Vehicles Renewed v1 (3684679695) before activating.
[*] [b]100% Compatible:[/b] Fully tested and operational with [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager)[/b], [b]More Network Capacity Renew[/b], [b]Improved Public Transport 2/3[/b], [b]Advanced Vehicle Options (AVO)[/b], and [b]Loading Screen Mod (LSM)[/b].
[*] [b]Safe Savegame Migration:[/b] Seamlessly loads existing cities created with older More Vehicles editions without any vehicle data loss.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]🔧 OPEN SOURCE & REPOSITORY[/h1]
Source code is open source and available on GitHub:
[b]GitHub:[/b] https://github.com/NqocDuy1426/MoreVehiclesRenew2

[hr][/hr]
